    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0146" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg40"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Conger</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    letter from Messrs. Charles Ahrenfeldt &amp; Son, of New York, in which they
                    complain that the government of the State of Amazonas imposes a tax of 5 per
                    cent on rubber from Peru in transit for New York down the Amazon River. As no
                    entry of the rubber is made at Manaos, it is claimed that the tax is
                    unreasonable and in violation of the practice of commercial nations. You will
                    inquire into the matter, and if the facts appear as stated make proper
                    representations against this tax.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d31-a1.xml" xpointer="d31-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
